    </p>

    <!-- AEO Quick Answer Block -->
    <div class="fzk-aeo-box" role="note" aria-label="Quick Answer">
      <p class="fzk-aeo-badge">Quick Answer</p>
      <p class="fzk-aeo-q"><strong>How much tax will I pay on a 401(k) withdrawal?</strong></p>
      <p class="fzk-aeo-text">
        A traditional pre-tax 401(k) withdrawal is generally included in taxable income. The federal tax you ultimately owe depends on your total income, filing status, deductions, credits, and other circumstances.
      </p>
      <p class="fzk-aeo-text" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
        If you take money out before the applicable early-distribution age or exception applies, an additional 10% tax may also apply. <strong>Your 401(k) provider may withhold federal income tax from the distribution (mandatory 20% default), but withholding is not necessarily the same as your final tax liability.</strong>
      </p>
